SET explanation = $res28$Based on the scenario, you are carrying out the Develop Team process. The source of the problem is that the training requirements were not correctly specified, resulting in wasted time and money. The immediate fix may require additional training with the associated loss of time and funds. But, in order to prevent the same issue from happening in the future, you need to revise the training requirements which are considered organizational process assets and are updated as an output of the Develop Team process. Note: It is likely that you will also want to add an entry in the lessons learned register; however, this option is not provided among the answer choices. Details for Each Option: A Request additional training funds Incorrect. Although additional training funds may be needed to meet the needs of the current project, this will not help correct the issue for future projects. B Perform updates to employee development plan records Incorrect. Performing updates to employee development plan records is strongly recommended in order to capture team members' development progress. However, doing so will not necessarily help future projects avoid the same issue. C Rewrite the project's training and evaluation documentation Incorrect. Any changes to the training and evaluation documentation of the current project will not necessarily help to prevent the training requirements mismatch from reoccurring in future projects. D Update training requirements in the company's learning and development system Correct. Training requirements can be documented by position, role, project type, or a variety of useful parameters. By updating requirements in the corporate system, you make the correct set available to future projects.$res28$,
